-- title:
--   Root bound before a block switches
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be a convex subset of a real normed space and consider an ordered tree with positive edge weights $w(c)$ summing to $1$ over each parent's children, path weights $\pi_k(v)$, and nonexpansive node maps $f_{k,v}:K\to K$. The tree is evaluated bottom-up: for values $H$ at level $k+1$, $\mathrm{collapse}(H)(p)=f_{k,p}\bigl(\sum_{\mathrm{par}(c)=p}w(c)H(c)\bigr)$, and $\mathrm{ev}_k(H)$ iterates collapse up to the root. Assume $\operatorname{diam}K\le1$. If an assignment $H$ at level $k$ has $\|H(v)-z\|\le e$ at a node $v$, and the proper ancestors of $v$ move $z$ by at most $e$ in total, then
--   $$
--   \|\mathrm{ev}_k(H)-z\|\le1-\pi_k(v)+2e .
--   $$
--
--   A root state whose focused node is near $z$ stays at distance about $1-\pi(v)$ from $z$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/openai/math/blob/1581d4cbdd69a0faf34b2089614fe2a814316a6a/lean/OAI/Analysis/Nonexpansive/BlockBefore.lean#L149-L167

